{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VS8SRJJQTQpsGcjB2cRh85","type":"tool_result","content":"  1590→        if moral_valence and moral_valence.valence:\n  1591→            constraint = MORAL_VALENCE_CONSTRAINTS.get(moral_valence.valence, \"\")\n  1592→            if constraint:\n  1593→                moral_valence_constraint = f\"\"\"\n  1594→\n  1595→MORAL VALENCE CONSTRAINT (Feature F3):\n  1596→This character has been classified as {moral_valence.valence.value} (confidence: {moral_valence.confidence:.0%}).\n  1597→{constraint}\n  1598→\n  1599→This is a HARD CONSTRAINT - your profile MUST respect this classification.\"\"\"\n  1600→\n  1601→        prompt = f\"\"\"Analyze the character \"{character.canonical_name}\" using ONLY the provided text evidence.\n  1602→\n  1603→The evidence below is sampled from throughout the entire narrative (early, middle, and late chapters).\n  1604→Your analysis should reflect the character's full arc, not just their initial appearance.{narrator_note}{summary_evidence_text}{moral_valence_constraint}\n  1605→\n  1606→Text Evidence:\n  1607→{context_text}\n  1608→\n  1609→CRITICAL REQUIREMENTS:\n  1610→1. Make ONLY claims that are directly supported by the provided text\n  1611→2. For each claim, provide the exact quote that supports it\n  1612→3. Consider how the character develops or changes throughout the narrative (if evident from the samples)\n  1613→4. If the text doesn't provide enough information about a trait or relationship, DO NOT invent it\n  1614→5. Distinguish between what the text explicitly states vs. what might be inferred\n  1615→\n  1616→Return a JSON response matching this example format exactly:\n  1617→\n  1618→```json\n  1619→{{\n  1620→  \"profile\": \"IMPORTANT: This must be PLAIN TEXT, not JSON. A brief 2-3 sentence description of the character based on provided evidence. The character is introduced as a young professional who recently moved to the area. They maintain close family connections and serve as an observer of unfolding events.\",\n  1621→  \"evidence\": [\n  1622→    {{\"statement\": \"Character is newly relocated\", \"quote\": \"I had just arrived in the city that spring\", \"position\": 1234}},\n  1623→    {{\"statement\": \"Has family in the area\", \"quote\": \"My cousin lived just across the bay\", \"position\": 2456}},\n  1624→    {{\"statement\": \"Observes others closely\", \"quote\": \"I found myself fascinated by their gatherings\", \"position\": 3789}}\n  1625→  ],\n  1626→  \"confidence\": 0.85,\n  1627→  \"limitations\": \"The provided context doesn't reveal the character's occupation, age, or long-term intentions in the area.\"\n  1628→}}\n  1629→```\n  1630→\n  1631→CRITICAL: The \"profile\" field must contain PLAIN TEXT only, not nested JSON structures.\n  1632→Return ONLY valid JSON matching the above structure. No other text.\"\"\"\n  1633→\n  1634→        # Helper to parse JSON from LLM response\n  1635→        def _parse_json_blob(s: str):\n  1636→            try:\n  1637→                return json.loads(s)\n  1638→            except json.JSONDecodeError:\n  1639→                start = s.find(\"{\")\n  1640→                end = s.rfind(\"}\")\n  1641→                if start != -1 and end != -1 and end > start:\n  1642→                    try:\n  1643→                        return json.loads(s[start:end + 1])\n  1644→                    except json.JSONDecodeError:\n  1645→                        return None\n  1646→                return None\n  1647→\n  1648→        # Retry loop: try up to 2 times on LLM errors\n  1649→        max_attempts = 2\n  1650→        for attempt in range(max_attempts):\n  1651→            try:\n  1652→                response = llm.query(prompt, system=CHARACTER_PROFILE_SYSTEM)\n  1653→                if response.success:\n  1654→                    # Clean up any thinking tags or extra formatting\n  1655→                    content = response.content.strip()\n  1656→\n  1657→                    # Try to extract JSON if wrapped in markdown code blocks\n  1658→                    if \"```json\" in content:\n  1659→                        content = content.split(\"```json\")[1].split(\"```\")[0].strip()\n  1660→                    elif \"```\" in content:\n  1661→                        content = content.split(\"```\")[1].split(\"```\")[0].strip()\n  1662→\n  1663→                    try:\n  1664→                        result = _parse_json_blob(content)\n  1665→                        if result is None:\n  1666→                            raise json.JSONDecodeError(\"Could not parse JSON\", content, 0)\n  1667→\n  1668→                        # Check if \"profile\" field itself contains JSON (double-encoded)\n  1669→                        profile = result.get(\"profile\", \"\")\n  1670→                        if profile and (profile.startswith(\"{\") or profile.startswith(\"[\")):\n  1671→                            # LLM returned nested JSON - try to parse it\n  1672→                            logger.warning(\n  1673→                                f\"Character profile for {character.canonical_name} contains nested JSON, attempting to parse\"\n  1674→                            )\n  1675→                            try:\n  1676→                                nested = json.loads(profile)\n  1677→                                if isinstance(nested, dict) and \"profile\" in nested:\n  1678→                                    # Double-encoded JSON\n  1679→                                    profile = nested[\"profile\"]\n  1680→                                    logger.info(f\"Successfully extracted profile from nested JSON for {character.canonical_name}\")\n  1681→                            except json.JSONDecodeError:\n  1682→                                # Not valid JSON - try to extract readable text\n  1683→                                logger.warning(f\"Nested JSON parse failed for {character.canonical_name}, extracting text\")\n  1684→                                profile = self._extract_text_from_malformed_json(profile)\n  1685→                                if not profile:\n  1686→                                    logger.warning(f\"Could not salvage text from malformed profile for {character.canonical_name}\")\n  1687→\n  1688→                        evidence = result.get(\"evidence\", [])\n  1689→                        confidence = float(result.get(\"confidence\", 0.5))\n  1690→\n  1691→                        # Validate evidence structure\n  1692→                        validated_evidence = []\n  1693→                        for ev in evidence:\n  1694→                            if isinstance(ev, dict) and \"statement\" in ev and \"quote\" in ev:\n  1695→                                validated_evidence.append({\n  1696→                                    \"statement\": ev[\"statement\"],\n  1697→                                    \"quote\": ev[\"quote\"],\n  1698→                                    \"position\": ev.get(\"position\", 0),\n  1699→                                    \"confidence\": \"high\" if confidence >= 0.7 else \"medium\" if confidence >= 0.4 else \"low\"\n  1700→                                })\n  1701→\n  1702→                        # If no valid evidence but we got a profile, mark as low confidence\n  1703→                        if profile and not validated_evidence:\n  1704→                            logger.warning(f\"Profile for {character.canonical_name} lacks evidence\")\n  1705→                            confidence = min(confidence, 0.3)\n  1706→\n  1707→                        return profile, validated_evidence, confidence\n  1708→\n  1709→                    except json.JSONDecodeError as e:\n  1710→                        logger.error(f\"Failed to parse JSON response for {character.canonical_name}: {e}\")\n  1711→                        logger.debug(f\"Raw content (first 500 chars): {content[:500]}\")\n  1712→                        # Try to extract readable text from malformed response\n  1713→                        salvaged = self._extract_text_from_malformed_json(content)\n  1714→                        if salvaged:\n  1715→                            logger.info(f\"Salvaged profile text for {character.canonical_name}\")\n  1716→                            return salvaged, [], 0.3\n  1717→                        return \"\", [], 0.0\n  1718→                else:\n  1719→                    # LLM returned error response\n  1720→                    error_msg = getattr(response, 'error', None) or 'unknown error'\n  1721→                    if attempt < max_attempts - 1:\n  1722→                        logger.warning(\n  1723→                            f\"LLM error for '{character.canonical_name}' (attempt {attempt + 1}/{max_attempts}): \"\n  1724→                            f\"{error_msg}, retrying...\"\n  1725→                        )\n  1726→                        continue  # Retry\n  1727→                    else:\n  1728→                        logger.error(\n  1729→                            f\"Profile generation failed for '{character.canonical_name}' after {max_attempts} attempts: \"\n  1730→                            f\"{error_msg}\"\n  1731→                        )\n  1732→                        return \"\", [], 0.0\n  1733→\n  1734→            except Exception as e:\n  1735→                if attempt < max_attempts - 1:\n  1736→                    logger.warning(\n  1737→                        f\"Exception generating profile for '{character.canonical_name}' (attempt {attempt + 1}/{max_attempts}): \"\n  1738→                        f\"{e}, retrying...\"\n  1739→                    )\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questio