{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929","id":"msg_014ZFVhDiGv9UNKfTrFgi8C7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"So even the Gatsby output doesn't have descriptions! This means profile generation isn't happening for any characters. The issue is more fundamental - profiles aren't being generated at all. \n\nLet me check if there's a flag or configuration that controls whether profile generation runs. Looking back at the code around line 1015, I see it checks `if llm:`. Let me verify if the LLM client is actually being passed to the analyzer. But wait - the EVALUATION_STATE says \"Character Profiles\" stage shows 0.0s duration and 0 LLM calls\". This means the stage is being executed but doing nothing.\n\nLet me re-read the profile generation code more carefully. The key is at line 1036-1039:\n\n```python\neligible_chars = [\n    c for c in pipeline_char_map.characters\n    if c.mention_count >= MIN_MENTIONS_FOR_PROFILE or getattr(c, 'is_narrator', False)\n]\n```\n\nMIN_MENTIONS_FOR_PROFILE is set to 5 at line 1014. Let me check what the mention counts are for the masque characters:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":263,"cache_read_input_tokens":87318,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":263,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f6180d44-b7c9-4a2d-b118-6d2a41dd4919","uuid":"85bd8748-b1cd-49e3-9023-47ba6b2f978e"}
